{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.784977Z","id":"3d0754961f02e911e6d20559ea1a4d68de3d4f7bd599c72235957d7ecdc5c4b8","body":{"detail":"lib/remote/models.dart Remote has id, origin, name, status and personName only. A display name with spaces reads oddly after '@'. Needs the core's remote record to carry the account login.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"acc0aa885f08b710c337e56ac200052c19e2cd335cc6d701ee56a84832fc637e"},"summary":"The publish sheet's \"as @login\" shows Remote.personName, the account's display name: Remote carries no login","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785015Z","id":"b4075175ae8836df02c2da4d5c664a6b99feabb19f5c9e76e94a4c03e2ff3202","body":{"detail":"lib/app.dart builds RemoteFlows without shareCopy, so Share… on the published sheet and the On clax.dev card falls back to openUrl. The in-app sharing sheet is not built yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":248},"content_hash":"8935e870fbbaaacbc95d96c09b2ef5c5db0fbedcfe9384848c3f339adfc166c8"},"summary":"Share… opens the copy's page in the browser while no shareCopy (the sharing sheet) is passed","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785046Z","id":"41456b47f3d49b4a5e7edea652931a31d47e83093a4036ca87bade5d72d9f075","body":{"detail":"lib/app.dart passes no connect to RemoteFlows. docs/contract.md's getApps() row says it signs in first when it is not; that holds only once connect is wired to the Settings › Sharing sign-in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"9da21845408019ee10acb84b8c989b4a2a1020843d86214603fc0af3f85f13fe"},"summary":"No sign-in hook is wired: with no connected remote, Publish and Get my apps show 'Connect to clax.dev in Settings › Sharing first.' instead of signing in","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785168Z","id":"2ae1a6f6591e0c99a1db7712682a6576456d5a9a7b64b1fb1f94d255e8a4f07e","body":{"detail":"RemoteCard reads RemoteFlows.headOf on initState and when the link's base changes. 404 shows 'No longer on <host>'; other failures show no pill. A shared, cached linked-app checker would let the card, the launcher and update offers agree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"ef8994c1fc99f6475ec7da678362697743194c462d85c46be81d1b7065766371"},"summary":"The On clax.dev card reads the head once per show; it does not poll, and its pill is the sync state computed here, not a shared checker's","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/library_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785540Z","id":"705a5e730af79982508d073ab4119b76c082d08cd28976177b1c144ab3502022","body":{"detail":"LibraryScreen calls pull(app) for each pick (RemoteFlows.getMyApps passes puller.pullFromLibrary with no confirm), so library apps install without the sheet that says who they are from, and a PullRefused's message is not shown in full.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"a172a38584fd5ef6a1335d6c5f07d8f21ecd6531eac13b5692c9d76c8c893e1e"},"summary":"Get on the library screen pulls the picked apps one after another without the install sheet; a failed pull shows only its row's short outcome","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/publish_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:06:11.765860Z","id":"839172325f1697a41cb76814b80c4c85f7b9331fa1930dbee3346f928133604c","body":{"detail":"publish_sheet.dart:134-139 build both lines from the version alone; _data (the Include my data switch) changes neither. A person who turns the switch on is told their data stays on the device while Publisher.publish (lib/remote/publisher.dart:132-137) exports it as the bundle's seed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"f97fcecadc7cd6e9378c2c6117e4f0a0cd15e7eab74c699feb8ff82126329b70"},"suggested_fix":"When _data is on, add the documents to the Goes up line and drop \"your data\" from Stays here.","summary":"With Include my data on, the publish sheet still says \"Stays here: your data, …\" and \"Goes up\" does not mention the documents","tags":["review","area:remote","copy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:06:11.767015Z","id":"f57c0db45f74db6e88db008ac84e78b0572842d5a9a19ff55096fdcf9957a131","body":{"detail":"_loadHead (lines 82-97) runs unawaited: any other error (a parse or IO failure from HttpRemoteApi) is an unhandled async error. When the head read answers 404 the pill says \"No longer on <host>\", but lines 186-213 still show New versions and Unpublish… for an author, whose Unpublish then fails against a copy that is not there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"733c8c8f7a01cf1a87c006cfa0f1b4bd7137690821e5b37abc472a78111d8c65"},"suggested_fix":"Catch Object in _loadHead (no pill), and hide the author controls while _gone.","summary":"The On clax.dev card catches only ClaxApiError from the head read, and still offers New versions and Unpublish… once the copy is gone","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/library_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:24.355205Z","id":"c141c2e9d89aa7979819b31209969aa0aaf9f850f3816f85ad06a9e0e9e316b8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b5195ebed","summary":"RemoteFlows.getMyApps passes confirm to pullFromLibrary, so each new app shows the install sheet (with its From line) first. test/ui/remote_flows_test.dart 'Get my apps asks with the install sheet, who it is from included, before it installs' passes (just test-affected a6028f8d2 at be347b362: 'Executed 239 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.') and failed without confirm.","supersedes":"705a5e730af79982508d073ab4119b76c082d08cd28976177b1c144ab3502022","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/publish_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:24.574466Z","id":"f0fac293ffe80e79f4b15d446420f3ea15f85d4eedd6a96566b0be68756ec672","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b5195ebed","summary":"With Include my data on, Goes up ends ' · your data' and Stays here reads 'earlier versions, threads, API key'. test/ui/publish_sheet_test.dart 'Include my data and Automatically are the person’s choice for this publish' checks both lines; it passes (just test-affected a6028f8d2 at be347b362: 'Executed 239 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.') and failed with the Goes up line left unchanged.","supersedes":"839172325f1697a41cb76814b80c4c85f7b9331fa1930dbee3346f928133604c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:24.948249Z","id":"1c0a99594155322c6d94e49f6d09a4b8748fe01aa0c5e9d750b775ea38719154","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b5195ebed","summary":"_loadHead catches any other error as no pill, and New versions and Unpublish… show only while the copy is there. test/ui/remote_card_test.dart 'a copy no longer there says so and offers no Unpublish' passes (just test-affected a6028f8d2 at be347b362: 'Executed 239 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.') and failed with the !_gone guard removed.","supersedes":"f57c0db45f74db6e88db008ac84e78b0572842d5a9a19ff55096fdcf9957a131","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:25.248019Z","id":"eb5ff5ec74db2f310059eebe3c56bfa240078a540f68a13c1a7e9e1d52a3fab0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"41456b47f3d49b4a5e7edea652931a31d47e83093a4036ca87bade5d72d9f075","summary":"docs/contract.md's getApps() row no longer says it signs in first (be347b362); the sign-in hook itself is still not wired.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:07:48.307456Z","id":"e9aa9fdd3490b8ce307be798a5778b620912b3316ae820f5354d8d6f13160c7f","body":{"detail":"failed() shows a new failure sheet only when context.mounted; the context is the screen that started the publish (the inspector, or the launcher's menu). Failure: close the sheet while offline, leave the inspector, and a Moved or Refused outcome when the connection returns is logged nowhere the person sees. A second publish queued behind a waiting one also shows no waiting step: onWaiting (remote_flows.dart:170-178) runs only when Publisher.waiting changes, and it already holds the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"4fa3b7369290d52d67b1e9e3c1f0537f60947a797be281edc036ba089a4e903c"},"suggested_fix":"Report a background outcome through the inbox or a toast on the root navigator, and set the waiting step at once when Publisher.waiting already holds the app.","summary":"A publish that fails after its sheet was closed is reported only while the calling screen is still mounted","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:01:47.839573Z","id":"25437d5353e9540c74d56cf0312ebc44f46f6f0c60bbb8b3d804d3e9df81c053","body":{"detail":"RemoteApi.share (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:347) sends {github_login, access} only, while the remote's put_share also takes {person} and the web dialog (web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte, change()) sends it. So suggest() here drops candidates without a github_login, subjectLogin() answers a named candidate's login (null when they have none, refused with the add field's message), and _person (share_sheet.dart:573-650) disables the three access items for a share whose githubLogin is null; Remove still works. Widening RemoteApi.share to take a person ID would let the sheet match the web dialog.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"d6d9054eaea5677e0a3b82529c74ceb868dca56000c8b7596da0069c7cd638f1"},"suggested_fix":"Give RemoteApi.share a person-or-login target, as hosted/api.ts share() takes, and drop the githubLogin filters here.","summary":"The Share sheet adds and changes people by GitHub login only: a suggested person with no login is not offered, and a share held by person alone cannot change role","tags":["sharing","app-push-pull","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:01:47.839823Z","id":"7d3fd136f494ec45307ae9bf6ec43c3dcc06e1dcef84bf4703069f1b2cc74570","body":{"detail":"share-model.ts has no COMMENTS_LABEL or COMMENTS_NOTE on this branch; docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-21-app-push-pull.md Task 6 (line 317) names them: COMMENTS_LABEL = \"Comments\", COMMENTS_NOTE = {on: \"People who can comment may comment.\", off: \"Off: nobody can comment, whatever their access.\"}. commentsLabel and commentsNote here copy those. When Task 6 lands, check the two still match word for word.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"3bdc6093428c30dd4d0c89294b81ddccf4c6968b3ed998a8b367b94d266187c2"},"summary":"The Comments switch's words are not in web/shell/src/ui/share-model.ts yet: taken from the plan's COMMENTS_LABEL and COMMENTS_NOTE","tags":["sharing","copy","app-push-pull","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:01:47.839923Z","id":"0368a095d8ef0b2efe5e52c680f9fef249c375de69188ce51cdb35f2bae7a8ab","body":{"detail":"test/ui/share_sheet_test.dart passes shareLink and copyText fakes. Unchecked: SharePlus.instance.share(ShareParams(text:, subject:, sharePositionOrigin:)) on Android, iPhone, iPad (popover anchored at the button) and the Mac's NSSharingServicePicker, and Clipboard.setData on each.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"db9945c2517fd7fd97ed6496cf2cbca79ac7057c5f960bbd288b766db1a28181"},"summary":"Share link… (share_plus with the link as text) has not run on a device; widget tests replace it","tags":["sharing","unverified","app-push-pull","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:10:20.839945Z","id":"ca4844b071b0c3e10aa3520177465cb257478b4c12f83123e05ef4c98f466bcc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:32f435697","summary":"RemoteFlows.share now opens showShareSheet (lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart) when no shareCopy is given; only a link with no remote ID opens the page. test/ui/share_sheet_test.dart 'entry points Share… on the inspector card opens the sharing sheet' asserts the sheet shows and openUrl is not called: just test-affected HEAD~2 -> //apps/clax_app:ui_share_sheet_test PASSED, 65 tests pass.","supersedes":"b4075175ae8836df02c2da4d5c664a6b99feabb19f5c9e76e94a4c03e2ff3202","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:15:20.421688Z","id":"3b8fcaa97f562e27b1e16abc023cd6bd8facf90c0690b7af3b5bcd247f345ca7","body":{"detail":"Failure: type the owner's own login and tap Add. put_share (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs, put_share) answers 400 already_owner \"that is this Clax's owner, who can already do everything\" (crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs, already_owner), and web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte act() shows that message; _failText here shows \"Couldn’t change who can open <title>.\" for every 400 (invalid_login, unknown_person, already_owner, invalid_args), so the person cannot tell what to fix.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":257},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"a435947f5986013dbd3ef4c46e05fb9ea0a9ebee6376fc6b45a7f3bb72b5c022"},"suggested_fix":"For a ClaxApiError with status 400, show its message (or map the three codes to app words).","summary":"A refused sharing change shows a generic line instead of the remote's reason","tags":["review","sharing","app-push-pull","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:15:20.423207Z","id":"9fb016d6294f88fa7f421f3fc2428a50d45e92fc78e1ea97bbe7f7425acae86e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"25437d5353e9540c74d56cf0312ebc44f46f6f0c60bbb8b3d804d3e9df81c053","summary":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.6 asks for an add field taking \"a GitHub login or a known name\". People with no GitHub login exist on a hosted Clax: redeem_invite_in_browser (crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:665-686) makes a person by invite alone, and share_candidates (crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:619-638) LEFT JOINs github_identities, so such a person is suggested with github_login null. The app can neither add them nor change their role (the access items are disabled with no line saying why); only the web dialog can.","tags":["review","sharing","app-push-pull","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:24:20.995948Z","id":"e517f1bae0b265f33ef0f5ed4fbf4f54dc50a4c57f78eb5889b4d7c7168814bf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:40e7ab437","summary":"RemoteApi.share takes a ShareTarget (SharePerson or ShareLogin; lib/remote/remote_api.dart) and sends {person} or {github_login}; the sheet offers every suggestion, adds a chosen or named candidate by person and changes access by person once known. test/ui/share_sheet_test.dart 'a suggested person with no GitHub login is added and their access changed by person' and 'a known name typed in full is that person, whose access then changes by person' fail with the login filter or a by-login row restored (target/t11b-mut2.log) and pass as committed: just test-affected 89edc6a8d -> 90 tests pass.","supersedes":"25437d5353e9540c74d56cf0312ebc44f46f6f0c60bbb8b3d804d3e9df81c053","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:24:21.077011Z","id":"b9263f92c672da3eb8e7649357b5dea07f7400ba2b04c731a620d01f0855e939","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:40e7ab437","summary":"_failText shows the remote's message for a 400 that carries one. test/ui/share_sheet_test.dart 'a refused add shows the reason the remote gives' (400 already_owner) fails with that line removed and passes as committed: just test-affected 89edc6a8d -> 90 tests pass.","supersedes":"3b8fcaa97f562e27b1e16abc023cd6bd8facf90c0690b7af3b5bcd247f345ca7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:26:22.875446Z","id":"0ea00e81e2d5ea01f6c9826229be129b4284914e828ed1c93cb7a685f2ceccd6","body":{"detail":"Commenting out `if (named.length > 1) return null;` (share_sheet.dart:134) left //apps/clax_app:ui_share_sheet_test passing. Failure under that mutation: with two suggestions both named \"Sam\", typing Sam and tapping Add shares with the stranger GitHub login `sam` instead of saying \"Type a GitHub login, such as @octocat, or pick someone.\"; web/shell/src/ui/share-model.ts subject() refuses it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"a1c3f736535dc0038814c1a5c16cdd7d4f35acf02ce2bab29c5906e2a6ee2b0a"},"suggested_fix":"A widget test with two candidates of one name: Add refuses and calls no share.","summary":"No test pins that a name two suggested people share is refused rather than taken as a GitHub login","tags":["review","tests","sharing","app-push-pull","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:04.115426Z","id":"b1f43881e1f9ed0db97af76619e11e3c7f8b77147b32c869996c6068008b2361","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3d0754961f02e911e6d20559ea1a4d68de3d4f7bd599c72235957d7ecdc5c4b8","summary":"Settings › Sharing has the same gap: its clax.dev row reads \"Connected as <person_name>\" and Publishing as shows person_name (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart _remoteLine and _remoteRows), not @login, for want of a login on Remote.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:08.600904Z","id":"dc165e324b89f3f986cdda03b4bb2ca3516c1e6766f59f5b506b5ada8ae7f77b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e8e2f223e","summary":"lib/app.dart passes _connect (the connect sheet) as RemoteFlows' connect hook (e8e2f223e), and docs/contract.md's getApps() row says it signs in first. just test-affected HEAD~3 at e8e2f223e: 'Executed 243 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.' (connect_sheet_test, settings_sharing_test and app_bundles_test among them).","supersedes":"41456b47f3d49b4a5e7edea652931a31d47e83093a4036ca87bade5d72d9f075","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:42:52.602248Z","id":"5574367630807ce93fc633d708b6afefa5c27ba92bc17def11203c2a7270b9ef","body":{"detail":"_connected(origin: link.remoteOrigin) finds no remote at that origin and calls the connect hook, which in lib/app.dart (_connect) always signs in to https://clax.dev. The answer is not at the link's origin, so `!at(r)` returns null and RemoteFlows.publish ends with no message (test/ui/remote_flows_test.dart 'a sign-in at another origin is not taken for a linked app' asserts that nothing is shown). Failure: an app got through clax:get?url=https://other.example/a/<id> (lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart artifactOf), then Publish to clax.dev… from its menu: the person signs in to clax.dev, or, signed in already, sees nothing at all.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"242b006b02744e1250137aac74af5e759ae7752d03d528e189fca6193371eebc"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the link's origin to the connect hook, or show 'Sign in to <host> first' (or the Refused for a recipient link) instead of returning silently.","summary":"Publish of an app linked at a hosted Clax other than clax.dev runs the clax.dev sign-in, then silently does nothing","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T13:38:29.121415Z","id":"261314f9b2664cb68b1018801f4bf7b9c876f67ce8bdbd6f40027189584f9142","body":{"detail":"DivergedSheet renders '<who> published vN (“note”) after this device’s vM.' when given a note (test/ui/diverged_sheet_test.dart 'names the head’s note when it has one'), but lib/remote/models.dart RemoteHead has no note field, so diverged() at these lines passes none and the parenthetical never appears. Needs the core's head read to carry the version's note.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"f47d2571940653c9571063e780c2ee20cad324a3a5fe823d61777959a673b658"},"summary":"The diverged sheet never shows the head's note: RemoteHead carries none, so DivergedSheet.note is never passed","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:46.380575Z","id":"123a68c83e4fd297aaaa6a492c7dc122112b8254c1728ff07e2037c3a168ddcc","body":{"detail":"An account that can comment only through the copy's link ('Anyone with the link can comment') holds no share. Its copy is missing from remote.apps(rid), so access stays null and Tell @owner is hidden, although spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.7 offers it to anyone who may comment. FakeRemoteApi.comment checks the copy's access, so the tests cannot see the gap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"e3c290ce32908318026321da73f25e2c1812157b06241f3a6f80abd05d930077"},"suggested_fix":"Read the caller's effective access from the head (or a route that answers it) instead of the apps list.","summary":"Tell @owner reads a non-author's right to comment from GET /api/remotes/{rid}/apps, which lists only owned and shared apps","tags":["review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:54:38.070485Z","id":"984cae3d9dfa4ddaedb1e684ad4b410a9973632060f848bcbf2c742f6a0ffa44","body":{"detail":"With no newer bundle waiting, the way back to Live is restoring the release in Versions or the next update. A card action that reinstalls the kept release (Take the public vN) is not built.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":211},"content_hash":"13937bb80d29a83c3e87d198f7d10367f2fa081e60e4b8567095b5f5f2c7705a"},"summary":"A recipient's fork has no 'Take the public vN' (reset) on its card; only Publish fork…","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:59:28.251747Z","id":"d0d73f16bfff9d43724746979b354d259383ff55d9fe997c17691dcd1031d86f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:adbf45b30","summary":"RemoteHead.note (lib/remote/models.dart) now reads the head's note and RemoteFlows.diverged passes it to DivergedSheet; the hosted head route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs) reports it. Evidence: //apps/clax_app:ui_remote_flows_test 'the diverged sheet names the head’s note' and //apps/clax_app:remote_remote_api_test pass; dropping 'note: head.note' fails the former; api_app_bundles::bundle_put_get_roundtrip_and_head passes with the note asserts. The core's /api/remotes/{rid}/artifacts/{raid}/head proxy must forward the field as well.","supersedes":"261314f9b2664cb68b1018801f4bf7b9c876f67ce8bdbd6f40027189584f9142","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102171Z","id":"9675cb14f6af7758c76cd6ce8c0a572ab579b06a927020903795901c21c36b07","body":{"detail":"Publisher keeps a pending upload as AppLink.pendingBundle plus the file <support>/publishing/<aid>.clax (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart:199-200). RemoteFlows.unpublish sets the link to null without Publisher._drop, and forgetDeleted (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart) forgets the entry without the file. Publisher.resume only visits entries whose link holds a pending bundle, so nothing deletes the file again: up to 32 MiB per app stays in the support directory.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":695},"end":{"line":705},"content_hash":"fcfa0848d4ed1efe3887bbb18f4eb3ae984f64a5cd617404ff982f46f235871f"},"suggested_fix":"Delete <support>/publishing/<aid>.clax in unpublish (through a Publisher method) and in forgetDeleted; resume can also sweep files whose app has no pending record.","summary":"Unpublish and app deletion leave a pending bundle's bytes in <support>/publishing/<aid>.clax for good","tags":["review","lifecycle","disk","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682492Z","id":"108a45be87c76d1860554f9e5dd9eb7103baa0437c932938721ee2bcbff4ad56","body":{"detail":"_start maps any ClaxApiError other than status 0 or remote_unreachable to the same retry line. POST /api/remotes answers a remote's refusal as 502 remote_refused with remote_code and remote_status (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:176-218), and those refusals are permanent: a clax.dev older than the client_kind change answers 400 invalid_json to the app's device-code request (record 24555b7b on crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:557-561: DeviceCodeBody is deny_unknown_fields), so every Connect, Publish and Get my apps sign-in shows this line and every Try again repeats it. The same line covers 400 invalid_args from the core (a URL that is not a public origin). test/ui/connect_sheet_test.dart has no test of a failed start: neither line is pinned.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"22242367025daaa6d5d9d14cc0949704ee4343beeb8818487938d47781744743"},"suggested_fix":"Branch on the code: remote_refused with remote_status 400 and remote_code invalid_json reads '<host> needs an update before this app can connect to it.' (no Try again); other remote_refused show the remote's own message without promising a retry helps; keep the retry line for status 0, remote_unreachable and 5xx remote_status. Add widget tests for each branch, driving FakeRemoteApi.addRemote with the 502 shapes the core returns.","summary":"The connect sheet answers every refused sign-in start with 'Couldn’t start signing in to <host>. Try again.', though Try again fails the same way","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682575Z","id":"742d7c242349de5eb3fc2bc071cdb67c32b70f1d1a8f87588fd20565153f1d96","body":{"detail":"The poll's catch continues on e.status >= 500. The core's POST /api/remotes/{id}/poll (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:200-223, public::poll_sign_in at crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:779-822) maps authorization_pending, slow_down, access_denied and expired_token, and turns any other refusal of the remote's /api/hosted/device/token (another 400 code, a 404 for a device code the remote no longer has, a 403) into 502 remote_refused, and a revoked or refused token into 502 remote_signed_out. Each of these is final, yet the sheet keeps showing the code until connectCodeLifetime passes and then shows 'That code expired. Try again.', which is not what happened.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"cee1beb278ed6e3c36a2a08389bda1987c9921dcab67ba9abace0c3679398210"},"suggested_fix":"Retry only on status 0, code remote_unreachable, or remote_refused whose remote_status is 5xx; treat any other remote_refused or remote_signed_out as 'Couldn’t finish signing in to <host>.' at once. Add a connect_sheet_test case for a 502 remote_refused with remote_status 400.","summary":"Polling treats every 5xx as 'ask again', but the core answers every remote refusal as 502, so a refused sign-in polls silently for 10 minutes and then says the code expired","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682609Z","id":"c5b81cc47de41f0a787e9991b28d1851a5d2f7a5426958167597f94c7675ae2c","body":{"detail":"widget.openAuth's answer is dropped (unawaited(widget.openAuth(s.verificationUrl))). ExternalLinks.openAuth (lib/platform/external_links.dart:32-35) answers false for a non-https verification URL, and the native side answers false when nothing could open it: Android EngineChannels.openAuth on ActivityNotFoundException (no browser), iOS AuthSession.open when ASWebAuthenticationSession.start() fails (ios/Runner/NativeChannel.swift). The sheet then still reads '<host> is open in your browser. Sign in there, then check that it shows this code:' (lines 263-266) with only the code; the verification URL is not shown or copyable, so the person has no way to reach the approval page except 'Open <host> again', which fails the same way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":173},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"0196174baafa586d48ba6748728f832b35000754dd5a56f5dce166e1d3e2b497"},"suggested_fix":"Keep openAuth's answer in state; when false, say '<host> didn’t open. Go to <verification URL> on any device and enter this code:' with the URL as SelectableText (and a Copy button), keeping Open again. Add a test with openAuth answering false.","summary":"The connect sheet says '<host> is open in your browser' whether or not the sign-in page opened, and never shows its address","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682670Z","id":"221ea7af4d3eaeac3aa437d0a5b14f204a15785980c5e04cdd9a7f4411886bd9","body":{"detail":"Failure: an author's app in Kept mine or Diverged, the device offline (or clax.dev answering 5xx), the person picks Publish as a new app (RemoteCard 'remote-new-app' or DivergedSheet 'diverged-new-app'). _resolve shows BundleProgressSheet with onCancel null for DivergeChoice.newApp, closable false, and dismissible: false. Merger.resolveDiverged runs Publisher.publishAsNewApp → _leaving → _queue → _publish, whose push goes through _retrying (lib/remote/publisher.dart:756-771), which retries a status-0 or non-final 5xx answer forever with backoff. The sheet shows 'Publishing <title> as a new app…' with no button and cannot be dismissed (lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart BundleProgressSheet: Close shows only with closable, Cancel only with onCancel), so the app is unusable until the network returns or the app is killed. publish() for the same situation passes closable: true and the waitingStep line (remote_flows.dart:213-230).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":456},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"862a03b515f96eed10bac800dade10260970741596e7003603063f743f553f70"},"suggested_fix":"For DivergeChoice.newApp pass closable: true (the publish goes on in the background, as publish() does) and listen to publisher.waiting to show RemoteFlows.waitingStep; or make the sheet dismissible. Add a remote_flows_test case: publish as new app with publish failing status 0, then Close is offered and closes the sheet.","summary":"Publish as a new app while offline leaves a modal progress sheet with no Close or Cancel until the connection returns","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682726Z","id":"52e76a1f1bed9b36241ec00435fb7b383f354bfda08edb1f4dd482ef36cef8cb","body":{"detail":"_failText checks e.unanswered (status 0) for 'Couldn’t reach <host>'. The app's RemoteApi goes through the in-process core, which answers an unreachable remote as 502 remote_unreachable and a token revoked on the remote as 502 remote_signed_out (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:176-218; crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs forward, lines 163-180), never status 0, so offline every change reads 'Couldn’t change who can open <title>.' and a revoked device is never told to connect again. _unread (lines 455-466) also uses _failText for the initial read, so a sheet that only failed to load says a change failed. test/ui/share_sheet_test.dart models offline as ClaxApiError(status: 0, code: unreachable) (lines 29-33), which the core does not return for a remote it cannot reach, so the tests pass against a fake that answers what the real path never does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"e86ec2f67dbed8dfc7b4565db99af8307c5fbefd1bf4d17735246b74bd6bded3"},"suggested_fix":"Treat code remote_unreachable like unanswered, and remote_signed_out as 'This device is signed out of <host>. Connect again in Settings › Sharing.'; give the load failure its own line ('Couldn’t read who can open <title>.'). Change the tests' _offline to the core's shape (status 502, code remote_unreachable) and add one for remote_signed_out.","summary":"The Share sheet's failure lines miss the core's real 'unreachable' answer, and a sheet that could not be read says 'Couldn’t change who can open <title>'","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682771Z","id":"a5478ac476290ff452f4a4df22c1efc5eae88cf7c11e0f3ad95b06e9d00b9ac3","body":{"detail":"unpublish (lines 682-686) shows 'Couldn’t reach <host>. <title> is still on it.' only for e.status == 0; tellOwner's post (lines 568-573) the same; LibraryScreen._load (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/library_screen.dart:61-68) shows 'Couldn’t reach <host>.' only for status 0. These calls go through the core's /api/remotes/... routes, which answer an unreachable remote as 502 remote_unreachable and a revoked token as 502 remote_signed_out (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:176-218; crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs:163-180 and unpublish at 601-650). Offline, Unpublish says 'Couldn’t unpublish <title>.', Get my apps 'Couldn’t read your apps on <host>.', and Tell @owner 'The comment wasn’t posted: <core message>'; a revoked device is never told to reconnect. Only connect_sheet.dart:163 checks remote_unreachable. test/ui/remote_flows_test.dart:23-27 models offline as status 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":676},"end":{"line":688},"content_hash":"a0760e918235aec5174a545d294fb2983cd7fb8f1e57a0bf16d3ad7c3fd51bfe"},"suggested_fix":"Add one helper beside userMessage (e.g. remoteUnreachable(e) => e.unanswered || e.code == 'remote_unreachable', and remoteSignedOut(e)) and use it in all four places, with a reconnect line for remote_signed_out. Switch the tests' offline error to 502 remote_unreachable.","summary":"Unpublish, Tell @owner and Get my apps test status 0 for 'Couldn’t reach', which the core never answers for an unreachable remote","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682925Z","id":"242476dd60ddd40f6fc7ff0ee6dd3068e2f81ffaf7b838b458f21f0f7af77b03","body":{"detail":"syncStateLabel ('☁ Live', '↑ Newer here', '↓ Update waiting', '⑂ Changed in both places', '⑂ Changed here') and versionMarkLabel in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart:20-24 ('☁ public', '☁ was public') put the glyphs in Text. The same branch avoids them elsewhere for this reason: working_chip.dart says the diverged pill is 'in words alone: ⑂ is not in the pill’s font', and SyncTileBadge in launcher.dart draws Material icons because 'the glyphs are not in every system font'. The card's Text has no semanticsLabel, so TalkBack/VoiceOver read 'cloud', 'upwards arrow' or 'OCR fork'. The pill Text also sits unconstrained after an Expanded in a Row (lines 156-169), so '⑂ Changed in both places' at 200% text on a 360 dp phone can overflow the card.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"7d5e1b2f7880184c6318b01081fb06201efeb881ebcdd5a6a460c55ef76b97de"},"suggested_fix":"Draw the glyph as the same Icon SyncTileBadge uses (ExcludeSemantics) followed by the words, give the Text a semanticsLabel without the glyph, and wrap the pill in Flexible with ellipsis (or move it under the title). Same for versionMarkLabel.","summary":"The On clax.dev card's pill and the Versions marks draw ☁ ↑ ↓ ⑂ as text, which the app's font may lack and screen readers read as symbol names","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682971Z","id":"8de3211a9d30c5a3bd18f341d3d28b7f5d5060e6cf8aee65c585070e3a657b81","body":{"detail":"The add row's _Choice (key share-add-access) and the General access pickers (share-general, share-link-access) pass no semanticLabel, so a screen reader hears a button named 'Can view' or 'Restricted' with nothing saying it sets the access of the person being added, who can open the app, or what anyone with the link may do; only the per-person pickers get 'Access for <name>' (line 635). The Versions tab's per-row Publish buttons (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart:179-184) are likewise all 'Publish', without the version they publish.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":587},"content_hash":"1a58e625e6d2dd6d928d2bee7002147a703353d45a8fa2184c0afcee6599ca6e"},"suggested_fix":"Give _Choice semanticLabels: 'Access for the person you add', 'General access', 'Access for anyone with the link'; give each Versions Publish a Semantics label 'Publish version N'.","summary":"The Share sheet's access pickers announce only their current value: 'Can view', 'Restricted'","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.466140Z","id":"6e2da63ab21d732c53865321d7ebead252dffae55f586c2c1417c3e2b6896a37","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart:161-166 picks between only two lines: e.unanswered || e.code == 'remote_unreachable' gives 'Couldn’t reach', and anything else gives 'Couldn’t start signing in to $_host. Try again.'. crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:194-218 (From<RemoteFail> for ApiError) turns every remote status into 502 remote_refused with remote_code/remote_status, so a permanent 400 from the remote gets the retry line. grep for failure cases in apps/clax_app/test/ui/connect_sheet_test.dart finds no test of a failed addRemote.","kind":"comment","references":"108a45be87c76d1860554f9e5dd9eb7103baa0437c932938721ee2bcbff4ad56","summary":"confirmed: every non-unreachable start failure gets the same 'Try again' line","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.466463Z","id":"1672bf244c5ab531769f02d3553406bfda0daf06cca9325aa4ae645a4c17013a","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart:189: `if (e.unanswered || e.status >= 500) continue;`. crates/clax-server/src/public.rs poll_sign_in (lines ~779-822) handles only 400 authorization_pending/slow_down/access_denied/expired_token, and `_ => Err(f.into())` / `Err(f) => Err(f.into())` go through From<RemoteFail> (public.rs:194-218), which always gives StatusCode::BAD_GATEWAY (remote_refused, or remote_signed_out for 401). The loop then runs until `until` passes and stops with _expired (connect_sheet.dart:178-182). apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart:749-753 already treats remote_refused and remote_signed_out as final for the same reason.","kind":"comment","references":"742d7c242349de5eb3fc2bc071cdb67c32b70f1d1a8f87588fd20565153f1d96","summary":"confirmed: poll retries the core's final 502 remote_refused/remote_signed_out until the code lifetime ends","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.466738Z","id":"d16446257e3a35f4f907f1ade1305566cfa9a237e1078eedfbeaf20fa4176324","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart:175 `unawaited(widget.openAuth(s.verificationUrl));` and :304 (Open again) ignore the answer. apps/clax_app/lib/platform/external_links.dart:32-35 answers false for a non-https URL; apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/NativeChannel.swift:121 `if !s.start()` is the iOS failure path. The body text at connect_sheet.dart:263-266 always says '$_host is open in your browser…'; grep -n verificationUrl apps/clax_app/lib/ui finds only those two openAuth calls, so the URL is never rendered.","kind":"comment","references":"c5b81cc47de41f0a787e9991b28d1851a5d2f7a5426958167597f94c7675ae2c","summary":"confirmed: openAuth's bool is dropped and the sheet never shows the verification URL","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.466995Z","id":"8e6e2f3b636eb6aca61af7fffd391ba0167bf4257a7c540b7dec5338a9fed3ce","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:466-477: for DivergeChoice.newApp onCancel is null, closable defaults false, dismissible: false. apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart:50-76 makes dismissible false into PopScope(canPop: false), isDismissible/enableDrag/barrierDismissible false. apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart:1107-1131 shows Close only if closable and Cancel only if onCancel. apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart:282-290 awaits publisher.publishAsNewApp → _leaving → _queue → _publish, whose push (publisher.dart:388) is in _retrying (publisher.dart:756-771), looping forever while _transient holds; offline the core answers 502 remote_unreachable (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:196-199), which _transient (publisher.dart:749-751) counts as transient. Compare remote_flows.dart:227-230, where publish() passes closable: true.","kind":"comment","references":"221ea7af4d3eaeac3aa437d0a5b14f204a15785980c5e04cdd9a7f4411886bd9","summary":"confirmed: Publish as a new app offline shows an undismissable sheet with no buttons until the network returns","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.467255Z","id":"f8a3176fdcc1ce21537233866a64e571a3331f1188fda6084de89afe63401818","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart:277 checks only e.unanswered; the fallback (line 289) is 'Couldn’t change who can open …'. _unread (line 456) calls _failText(_loadError!). RemoteApi.sharing/share/setLink go to /api/remotes/<rid>/artifacts/<raid>/sharing… (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:390-431, _copy at 458-459); the core's forward (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs:163-180) maps a send failure through ApiError::from(RemoteFail) to 502 remote_unreachable (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:196-199) and a remote 401 to 502 remote_signed_out (remote_apps.rs:128-137). apps/clax_app/test/ui/share_sheet_test.dart:29-33 models offline as status 0.","kind":"comment","references":"52e76a1f1bed9b36241ec00435fb7b383f354bfda08edb1f4dd482ef36cef8cb","summary":"confirmed: _failText misses 502 remote_unreachable/remote_signed_out and the load failure reuses the change-failed line","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.467518Z","id":"5581749a99d96e48825014619869bab263703fa3b635af6e7957115a2b138082","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:684 (`e.status == 0`), :571 (`ClaxApiError(status: 0)`), apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/library_screen.dart:63 (`e.status == 0`). These call /api/remotes/<rid>/artifacts/<raid> (DELETE), …/comments and /api/remotes/<rid>/apps (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:310-311, 379-380, 434-436). The core's unpublish (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs:601-650) maps a send failure with .map_err(ApiError::from) → 502 remote_unreachable (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:196-199); forward (remote_apps.rs:163-180) does the same. apps/clax_app/test/ui/remote_flows_test.dart:23-27 models offline as status 0.","kind":"comment","references":"a5478ac476290ff452f4a4df22c1efc5eae88cf7c11e0f3ad95b06e9d00b9ac3","summary":"confirmed: Unpublish, Tell @owner and Get my apps key 'Couldn’t reach' on status 0, which the core's remote routes never return","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.468314Z","id":"c2a14c0fee2ff75a96ccd9aa28d407b609182ca2fdf60f033e2c28bc0d3e25e5","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart:19-27 (syncStateLabel glyphs), :156-169 (Row: Expanded title then a plain Text(pill) with no semanticsLabel, Flexible or overflow). apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart:20-24 ('☁ public', '☁ was public'). apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart:393 documents '⑂ is not in the pill's font'; apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart:683 notes glyphs not in every system font.","kind":"comment","references":"242476dd60ddd40f6fc7ff0ee6dd3068e2f81ffaf7b838b458f21f0f7af77b03","summary":"confirmed: pill and version marks put ☁ ↑ ↓ ⑂ in Text, unlabelled, and the pill is unconstrained in its Row","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.468580Z","id":"accf7b748dd1a9a80e29539f4bf89b824e23c675f103000cb4d80569d565a458","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/share_sheet.dart:533-541 (share-add-access), :566-574 (share-general), :576-586 (share-link-access) pass no semanticLabel; only :632-635 does ('Access for $name'). _Choice wraps in Semantics only when semanticLabel is set (:707-709). apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart:179-184: every row's TextButton child is const Text('Publish'). The 'General access' heading (share_sheet.dart:561) precedes the pickers in reading order but is not part of the button's label.","kind":"comment","references":"8de3211a9d30c5a3bd18f341d3d28b7f5d5060e6cf8aee65c585070e3a657b81","summary":"confirmed: three _Choice pickers and the Versions Publish buttons carry no semantic label beyond their value","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
